{"tool_name":"human-cytoplasm-nucleus-translocation-assay-using-cellprofiler","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>In this human cytoplasm-nucleus translocation assay, learn how to load a previously calculated illumination correction function for two separate channels, measure protein content in the nucleus and cytoplasm, and calculate the ratio as a measure of translocation. This is a clumpy cell type, so studying the settings in primary object identification may be helpful for users interested in the more advanced options that module offers. More about these images can be found at the BBBC.</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>In this human cytoplasm-nucleus translocation assay, learn how to load a previously calculated illumination correction function for two separate channels, measure protein content in the nucleus and cytoplasm, and calculate the ratio as a measure of translocation. This is a clumpy cell type, so studying the settings in primary object identification may be helpful for users interested in the more advanced options that module offers. More about these images can be found at the BBBC.</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2020-03-03T19:45:43+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2014-12-08T14:46:08+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[{"target_id":4555,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"c15752d9-9193-4de3-8ab9-72cb325dd6e5","url":"/taxonomy/term/4555"}],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1505205189,"last_comment_uid":164,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"Cellprofiler team"}],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[],"has_documentation":[],"has_doi":[],"has_entry_curator":[{"target_id":98,"target_type":"user","target_uuid":"2ae7ecac-ed23-4375-8a06-79f6a294e65b","url":"/user/98"}],"has_function":